-- ============================================================
-- Alonecraft 4.61 -- Rogue / Subtlety, part 5
--   Master of Deception -> agility is 33/66/100% better at giving dodge
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md:
--   "Master of Deception: Your agility is 33/66/100% more effective at
--    increasing your dodge chance, and (as today)."
--
--
-- 13958 / 13970 / 13971
--
--   Effect1 (MOD_STEALTH_LEVEL) is untouched -- that is the "as today" half.
--   The new half goes in the free effect-2 slot as MOD_DODGE_PERCENT (49).
--
--   There is no aura in this core that multiplies the agility-to-dodge
--   conversion.  Player::GetDodgeFromAgility (Player.cpp:5126) reads the
--   GtChanceToMeleeCrit ratio table and a pair of file-local class tables,
--   and has no aura hook of any kind.  SPELL_AURA_MOD_RATING_FROM_STAT
--   (220) is not a substitute either: it grants dodge *rating*, which goes
--   through diminishing returns, so "33% more effective" would not mean 33%.
--
--   So the amount is computed in C++ (spell_rog_master_of_deception,
--   RogueMasterOfDeception.cpp), which calls GetDodgeFromAgility -- a public
--   method -- and takes a percentage of the agility-derived part.
--
--   EffectBasePoints2 carries the per-rank percentage (32/65/99 -> 33/66/100
--   after the usual +1 from DieSides), and the script reads that incoming
--   value rather than switching on spell ID.  Same data-driven rank map the
--   warlock talents use.
--
-- ============================================================


